# lockstep_requant -- two requant (COLS = 4), stream after the table is written: out_valid equal, out_q equal while valid
# Every input free and shared, tbl_fault_inject = 0, in_valid only once all four entries have been written (the tables
# are not reset): neo_core's rq_err never fires without a fault. Full proof by k-induction (drop 0.41) at PW = 32 with
# the table multiplier narrowed to MW = 4: at MW = 16 the induction step holds two 32x17 multipliers on equal inputs, an
# identical-circuit miter none of yices / bitwuzla / z3 / abc pdr closes in 150 s (a two-register micro test times out
# the same way), while the property does not depend on the width -- the copies compute one function. README.md.
# Drop 0.43: the copies' clock enables equal every cycle (the gate's formal model neo_icg_formal.sv, ungated).
[options]
mode prove
depth 2

[engines]
smtbmc yices

[script]
plugin -i slang
read_slang -DFORMAL -G MW=4 --top lockstep_requant_fv neo_icg_formal.sv requant.sv lockstep_requant_fv.sv
prep -top lockstep_requant_fv

[files]
formal/neo_icg_formal.sv
rtl/requant.sv
formal/lockstep_requant_fv.sv
